WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.568 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Mike Schur, who created
"The Good Place,"

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
and who you had
worked with before --

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.238 line:92%
You worked with him on "Parks.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
He had this idea
really laid out.

00:00:06.439 --> 00:00:09.676
And I think he knew from the
beginning that this would not be

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.311 align:start size:94% position:6%
a show that would be on
for gratuity.

00:00:11.311 --> 00:00:14.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Forever. He's like, "This sho
one day is gonna end."

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:16.349 line:92%
And I was like, "Be optimistic."

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:17.584 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, he did.

00:00:17.584 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
He always had an idea of
how it was gonna end.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:22.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think any of us foresa
it happening so quickly.

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:22.455 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yep.

00:00:22.455 --> 00:00:24.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But the reality is, you know,
is in television --

00:00:24.924 --> 00:00:26.960 align:start size:94% position:6%
Most writers in television
you guys, like,

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:30.296 align:start size:94% position:6%
episode 17 through 21,
they're like, "It's fluff.

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:32.032 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just get us to the ending.
-Yeah.

00:00:32.032 --> 00:00:34.667 size:84% position:42%
-So I really like these
encapsulated seasons

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:36.302 line:92%
where it's 12 or 13 episodes

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.170 size:88% position:44% line:92%
It gets people to watch.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
He figured out what the ending
should be

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:41.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he thought
we could draw it on foreve

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:43.209 line:92%
and some people might taper of

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:46.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause, you know, next episode
"Jason loses his shoes."

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, you don't want to follow
that plot line.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:51.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it's also
a little bit of a metaphor

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:54.621
about the human experience
is that it's over too soon

00:00:54.621 --> 00:00:56.856 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it leaves you
wanting a lot more.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience aws ]
-And it will be very --

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm excited to watch it,
but also we're going to then

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:04.397 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
live talk about it.

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm gonna host a thing with yo
and the rest of the cast.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm so thrilled
that you're doing that.

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:10.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It'll be a blast.
-All of us will be here.

00:01:10.637 --> 00:01:12.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
We'll all be,
like, crazy weeping.

00:01:12.539 --> 00:01:13.173 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Especially D'Arcy.

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.075 align:start size:94% position:6%
Watch it if anything
for the way D'Arcy cries.

00:01:15.075 --> 00:01:15.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's so cute.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:18.311 size:78% position:39%
-One of the things --
because I have heard,

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:20.080 align:start size:94% position:6%
obviously people my age
love this show.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:23.583
But I have heard that kids lov
this show because it talks about

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.585 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of things
that people don't know

00:01:25.585 --> 00:01:27.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
how to talk to kids about,
things like death

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:30.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
and what happens
when a loved one moves on.

00:01:30.824 --> 00:01:31.257 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:31.257 --> 00:01:31.958 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Is this something --

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.360
Have you started talking t
your kids about that yet?

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:36.830 size:78% position:39%
-Yeah, we did have --
Well, yeah, actually.

00:01:36.830 --> 00:01:39.833
We -- Our daughter when she wa
five said, "Am I gonna die?"

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:42.635
And we both -- like, the air got
sucked out of the room.

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:44.804 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were like, "This is it.
What do we do?

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.974 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are so many roads.
Like, do we make up a story?

00:01:47.974 --> 00:01:48.675 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Do we say we don't know?

00:01:48.675 --> 00:01:51.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do we say we know
and then actually not know?"

00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:53.246 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we just said,
"Yes, you're gonna die."

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she went, "Ugh."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:58.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then we said,
"And we really don't know

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.953 line:92%
what happens when you die.

00:01:59.953 --> 00:02:01.921 line:92%
You may just become flowers.

00:02:01.921 --> 00:02:04.791 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And she went..."Okay."

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.325 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.192 line:92%
And we were, like, so relieved

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:08.595
Because we did make a commitment
never to lie to them.

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:11.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's, like, controversia
'cause we also --

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.198 line:92%
They asked about Santa Claus

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"I'm not gonna lie to you.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:15.201 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He's dead.

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:16.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He's dead.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:19.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we don't know --
He's flowers.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:20.473 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Now he's flowers.

00:02:20.473 --> 00:02:21.941 line:92%
But I think because of that,

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:25.378
our kids have adopted this ver
practical sense about the world.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:28.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, like, recently
their grandfather was dying.

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.349 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And he's already passed,

00:02:29.349 --> 00:02:32.385 align:start size:94% position:6%
but while he was dying,
my little girl was in the back

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she said when,
"So, when Papa dies,"

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:35.955 line:92%
'cause we knew it was days

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.324 size:78% position:39%
"Are we going to come
to Oregon with you?"

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:40.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"Yeah, you'll come."

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:41.394 size:75% position:38% line:92%
And she said, "Okay.

00:02:41.394 --> 00:02:45.031
Do I need to bring my shovel
because I have a garden set.

00:02:45.031 --> 00:02:45.565 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.565 --> 00:02:47.934 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I said, "Why would you pac
your shovel, honey?"

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
She goes,
"Well, I want to help bury him

00:02:50.036 --> 00:02:52.772 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where do we do it?
The side of the house or..."

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:53.306 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:56.442 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, so practical,
and, like, wanted to help.

00:02:56.442 --> 00:02:59.112
And then I had to explain to her
we -- you know,

00:02:59.112 --> 00:03:01.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
we don't bury him
on the side of the house

00:03:01.281 --> 00:03:03.483 align:start size:94% position:6%
because it's not legal, but --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.483 --> 00:03:07.887
She genuinely wanted to,
like, bury her grandfather

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:11.090 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought, like, there's
something weirdly,

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.058 line:92%
oddly beautiful about that

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:15.495 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, she's a younger member o
the family contributing

00:03:15.495 --> 00:03:17.897 size:75% position:38%
to an older member's
peaceful passing on.

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.567 size:84% position:42%
-Yes, there's a real
circle of life to that.

00:03:20.567 --> 00:03:22.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Some people could say
she's a sociopath.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.303 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-I don't --

00:03:23.303 --> 00:03:24.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
I'm not going down that route.

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:26.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think it would have bee
worth hearing

00:03:26.105 --> 00:03:28.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
what she was saying
as she was throwing dirt on.

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:29.242 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Right, right, sure.

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:30.043 line:92%
-That might have revealed, like,

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:31.911 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot more than what
we're talking about now.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.279 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is so wonderful
to have you here.

00:03:33.279 --> 00:03:34.681 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to see you tomorrow.
-Yes.

00:03:34.681 --> 00:03:35.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I can't wait for that.
-I'm so happy.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:38.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you so much for letting
me be a part of that.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:40.420 size:88% position:44%
[ Cheers and applause ]
Kristen Bell, everybody.

